Copy of the host files cores/ddt_mandel/mono/build_mono.tcl reads: the HDMI chain only (no RISC-V, no DDR2, no network), taken from cores/diag/mono/host (T164 3a Q1 copy of host/ at commit aa45528c2,
branch t164, hdmi_timing fix included; the HDMI files of diag are the host's of that commit, T253's change is in top.v / app_i2c.v only and touches none of these).
T164 3a Q1 (Alex, 2026-11-01): "Copies instead." A change in host/ does not move this core's cache key or its build; a host fix reaches this core only by copying it in here on purpose,
then update this line. The files need not equal host/ (no lint compares them).
Edits to the copies: hdmi_modes.vh is ddt_hdmi_modes.vh (cdce_mode.v and hdmi_timing.v include that name: Vivado runs in host/, where an include of "hdmi_modes.vh" could read host/hdmi_modes.vh
instead of this copy). Nothing else. hdmi_enc/ is the host's fork of vendor/icepi/hdmi (the three unforked files come from the vendor tree, build_mono.tcl).
The core's own HDMI top (mono/ddt_hdmi.v) is hdmi_out.v of the host without the mode request, VIC scaler, overlay, pixel layer and freeze text; the clock chain and the synthesizer's I2C of mono/top.v are
those of the host's top.v.

